{"name":"High Tea","hex":"#7f6f57","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"high tea","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A late afternoon or early evening meal, typically consisting of a cooked dish with bread and butter and tea. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Formal afternoon tea."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high_tea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tea (meal)","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an umbrella term for several different meals consisting of food sometimes accompanied by tea to drink. The English writer Isabella Beeton, whose books on home economics were widely read in the 19th century, describes meals of various kinds and provides menus for the \"old-fashioned tea\", the \"at-home tea\", the \"family tea\", and the \"high tea\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Afternoon_meal_in_Tiffin.jpg/330px-Afternoon_meal_in_Tiffin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea_(meal)","wikidata":"Q245009"},{"title":"Tea","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an aromatic beverage prepared by infusion of hot or boiling fresh water with fresh or cured leaves of Camellia sinensis, an evergreen shrub native to East Asia that originated in the borderlands of southwestern China, northeast India and northern Myanmar. Tea has a stimulant effect in humans primarily due to its caffeine content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg/330px-Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea","wikidata":"Q6097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg/500px-Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/